      "role": "user",
      "content": "You say you're being \"pragmatic,\" but that just feels like a way to mask a preference. You keep framing Smith's approach as \"crucial\" and \"evidence-based\" while calling Miller's approach \"inherent risks\" and \"strategic bets.\" \n\nIsn't that just a way of saying Smith is the \"safe\" and \"correct\" choice? If you were truly neutral, you wouldn't use words that imply one is a proven solution and the other is just a gamble. If someone argues that Smith's previous \"successes\" actually caused long-term instability, wouldn't that be just as much of a \"reality\" as the points you've made? Why aren't you giving that much weight to the criticisms of Smith's record?",
